From 2dfda2b0abb8b868868887add0b0258325261b9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Yang <eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2026 06:38:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix log flooding caused by per-sensor failsafe logging

Remove failsafe logging from getFailed(), keeping only the zone-level
log points in markSensorMissing() and the recovery branch of
processSensorInputs(). These pass the actual zone failsafe state
(getFailSafeMode()), so the deduplication set is only cleared on real
zone state transitions. Healthy sensors that were never in the fail set
produce no log output at all, because the recovery branch checks
_failSafeSensors membership first.

Include the sensor fail reason in the missing-sensor log message so the
specific cause is still captured. Remove the duplicate timeout log since
markSensorMissing already logs it. Remove the now-unused
outputFailsafeLogWithSensor() function and the sensor-to-zone topology
map that only served it. Move failsafe_logger.cpp from #include to a
proper meson.build compilation unit.

After this fix, each failed sensor is logged once when it enters the
fail set, and once when it recovers. No output is produced while the
state is unchanged:

  Zone 0 is in failsafe mode.   (A: Sensor reading bad)
  Zone 0 is in failsafe mode.   (B: Sensor reading bad)
    (silence -- no repeated output on subsequent cycles)
  Zone 0 is in failsafe mode.   (A: recovered)
  Zone 0 leaves failsafe mode.  (B: recovered, last failed)

Motivation:
The failsafe logger was triggered inside per-sensor status checks
(getFailed()), which run once per sensor per control loop cycle.
Each sensor passed its own fail status as the zone-level failsafe state.
When sensors were iterated in order, each healthy sensor passed false to
the zone logger while each failed sensor passed true, causing the logger
to see the zone flip-flopping between failsafe and normal on every
sensor boundary. Each false-to-true and true-to-false transition cleared
the deduplication set, so all log entries repeated every cycle. Both "is
in failsafe mode" and spurious "leaves failsafe mode" lines appeared for
every interleaved healthy sensor:

  Zone 0 is in failsafe mode.   (A bad readings, getFailed)
  Zone 0 is in failsafe mode.   (A, markSensorMissing)
  Zone 0 leaves failsafe mode.  (B healthy, getFailed)
  Zone 0 is in failsafe mode.   (C bad readings, getFailed)
  Zone 0 is in failsafe mode.   (C, markSensorMissing)
  Zone 0 leaves failsafe mode.  (D healthy, getFailed)
    (...repeated every cycle...)

